---
const areas = [
  {
    title: 'Frontend',
    body:
      'Angular since the early days: I rewrote Rydoo’s WebForms app into an Angular SPA, co-built its component library and later led the frontend on an Nx monorepo. At VAB I built the new vab.be with Angular SSR on a headless CMS. I care about code a team can keep working in.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Backend',
    body:
      'C# and .NET since 2012: Web APIs, backend-for-frontend layers, SQL Server, and integrations with whatever the business runs on. Exact Online, Dropbox, Sitecore, and at Citymesh a brand-new mobile network core.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Working with AI',
    body:
      'At Citymesh I designed the workflow our frontend rebuild runs on: a chain of Claude Code skills that takes each screen from analysis to a merged pull request, with a review at every step. The AI drafts, I decide what ships. Colleagues now come to me when they want to work this way too.',
  },
];
---

<section id="work" class="border-t border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-16 md:py-28">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">What I do</h2>
    <div class="space-y-12">
      {
        areas.map((a) => (
          <div class="max-w-[62ch]">
            <h3 class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3 text-xl font-bold">
              <span class="stem" aria-hidden="true" />
              {a.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">{a.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* a tiny stem from the logo: vertical bar ending in a 30° cut */
  .stem {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 20px;
    background: var(--red);
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 3.46px), 0 100%);
  }
</style>
